{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415533-homebrew-boss-monster-the-behemoth-of-blades","id":1415533,"title":"[Homebrew Boss Monster] The Behemoth of Blades","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-26T07:13:18-07:00","id":1415533,"title":"[Homebrew Boss Monster] The Behemoth of Blades","content":"In the vain of &quot;Melee (Swords) is boring&quot; and &quot;What disgusting boss monster can I use to challenge my Solars?&quot; may I present... The Beast of Blades:<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>The Beast of Blades</b></u><br /> <br /> In the deserts of the South East, just beyond Prasad\u2019s western boarder lies a great crater named Mount Omelas. Why this vast caldera, which dips a great gouge in the desert, is called a mountain is long lost to time.<br /> <br /> In the middle of the caldera sits the Beast of Blades. Roughly the size and shape of a six-legged elephant, the Beast is sedentary to the point of practically being sessile. The Beast is a mindless construct, built an age ago by a long forgotten hero who wished to prove their supremacy with the blade. Both the Shogunate of antiquity and the present day kingdom of Prasad choose to leave the Beast well alone \u2013 for it does not leave its caldera, and no known magics can compel it to action beyond that which it was designed for.<br /> <br /> The Beast of Blades exists for one purpose, and one purpose only: to best those that challenge it to combat. Few in the Second Age have ever thought to prove themselves against the Beast: occasionally an overconfident Ifrit or a Gauda Bird seeking an honorable death might stumble upon it, but it has not been bested in over a thousand years.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Mount Omelas</b></u><br /> <br /> Mount Omelas is a vast crater, medium range from side to side. The twenty foot high lip of the crater rises another range-band, and the smooth, yet razor sharp, volcanic rock of the crater wall is a challenging climb (Difficulty 3).<br /> <br /> Omelas is an inhospitable place, as deadly as any in the Southern desert. The heat of the day and the cold of the night are truly oppressive (imposing a -0 to -3 penalty on actions and static values depending on season and time of day), and Omelas is frequently wracked by severe sandstorms, regardless of how calm the weather may be outside of the caldera.<br /> <br /> Mount Omelas lies on a fault line \u2013 a convergence of Earth and Fire essence. When mighty attacks of the Chosen crack the obsidian ground, geysers of steam or lava risk being released to the surface.<br /> <br /> The Beast of Blades never leaves Mount Omelas: no magic nor mundane force can be used to remove it.<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Beast of Blades</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Essence:</b> 4; <b>Willpower: </b>7; <b>Join Battle:</b> 14 dice (Base Initiative 7)<br /> <b>Health Levels:</b><br /> -0 x7 [ ] [ ] [ ] [ ] [ ] [ ] [ ]<br /> -1 x7 [ ] [ ] [ ] [ ] [ ] [ ] [ ]<br /> -2 x7 [ ] [ ] [ ] [ ] [ ] [ ] [ ]<br /> -4 x7 [ ] [ ] [ ] [ ] [ ] [ ] [ ]<br /> Incap [ ]<br /> <br /> <b>Actions:</b> The Beast of Blades has 14 dice on any action relating to its function as the ultimate proving tool for masters of the sword, and its actions may oppose rolls which can normal only be opposed by magic. It has 0 dice for any other action. Likewise, its static values are 7 or 0.<br /> <br /> Appearance 7 (Hideous), Resolve 0/7, Guile 0/7<br /> <br /> <b>Combat </b><br /> Attack (Blades): 14 dice (Damage 14, OVR 7)<br /> Grapple: 0 dice (14 dice to control)<br /> Combat movement: 14 dice<br /> Evasion 7, Parry 8<br /> Soak 14 Hardness 7<br /> <br /> <b>Merits and Charms</b><br /> <br /> Automaton<br /> <br /> Legendary Size<br /> <br /> Blade Beast (Permanent): The Beast Of Blades does not ever take proactive hostile action. It sits motionless in the center of Mt Omelas until challenged. It does not ever use its Combat Action to attack (though it may Aim or take Full Defense), and it moves only to gain advantage over its challengers \u2013 Rushing retreating foes or Disengaging when overwhelmed.<br /> <br /> As recompense, the Blade Beast may Clash any attack made against it (with a Withering or Decisive Clash). Its weapons are always \u201cin range\u201d when attacking, able to strike back at any point in Creation, and it need not be aware of an attack in order to Clash it.<br /> <br /> Turn the Blade (1WP; Reflexive; Instant; Uniform): When the Beast of Blades loses a Clash, it may pay 1WP to apply its Parry (minus Onslaught and Clash penalties) against the Threshold Successes of its attacker. If the Beast\u2019s Parry is higher, it successfully defends against the attack and takes no damage as if it had parried normally. This Charm\u2019s Willpower cost is waived against any foe attacking from the caldera\u2019s lip (or further away), any foe flying in the air, or any attack made with a sword.<br /> <br /> Vengeance Cut (1WP; Reflexive; Instant; Decisive Only, Counterattack): When the Beast of Blades is hit by an attack, it may respond with a Decisive Counter Attack or Disarm Gambit. The Beast's current Onslaught penalty is applied to its target's Parry. If the Beast successfully disarms a sword, it gains 1WP and 2i.<br /> <br /> Regenerate (1WP; Simple; Until hit by an attack): The Beast of Blades may spend 1WP to enter a healing state. It immediately heals one level of Bashing or Lethal damage. Further at the end of every round where the Beast is not successfully hit by a Withering or Decisive attack (or Gambit) it heals one further level of damage (of any type, including Aggravated damage). Being hit by an attack immediately ends this Charm.<br /> <br /> Further, if the Beast is ever slain, it may be fully repaired instantaneously when a master sword-fighter (4 or more dots in Melee or a sword-style Martial Art) sacrifices their sword to the Beast, plunging it into the creature\u2019s remains (where it is absorbed by the Beast, adding to the Beast\u2019s arsenal).<br /> <br /> The Art of Cutting (1WP; Supplemental; Instant; Decisive Only): The Beast of Blades converts the dice from Aiming into non-Charm successes and may re-roll 1s on a Decisive attack. The attack also ignores Hardness. The Supplemented attack may not be parried by a sword (it is Unblockable to swords), and doubles-7s if Clashed with a sword.<br /> <br /> Sword Body: The Beast\u2019s body is made of swords of all sizes, from blades the size of needles to a Warstrider-sized sword: the Beast of Blades may attack any sized foes, ignoring the defensive benefits of Merits such as Tiny Creature or Legendary Size. The Beast of Blades may also strike Immaterial beings.<br /> <br /> Element Resisting Prana: The Beast of Blades negates all environmental penalties and eliminates the deleterious effects of exposure to extreme climates. Environmental damage is reduced by 7.<br /> <br /> Lessons In Steel (Permanent; Eclipse): Fighting the Beast of Blades is considered a form of Training. Time spent fighting the Beast of Blades can be counted towards training Melee or any sword-based Martial Art (like Steel Devil Style), including Melee or Martial Arts Charms and sword-themed Specialties. Besting the Beast of Blades with a sword bleeds off a single point of Limit and allows the victor to train a sword-based Specialty, Charm, or Ability increase instantly (upon spending the requisite XP). This Charm itself may be learned as an Eclipse Charm, but the Limit reduction aspect does not apply if the Charm is learned by an Exalt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-05-2020, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T12:35:56-07:00","id":1416889,"title":"","content":"<i>I might try this.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T15:25:57-07:00","id":1416904,"title":"","content":"I like it, it puts up fight but you don't NEED to cheese it. Maybe specify that clashing any attack includes attacks it's not aware of so stealthmonkeys don't have to have it to easy. <br /> <br /> It might be a little weak on damage against anyone with resistance charms. Given that you can stop fighting it at any time if you are losing it could stand at least double 10s on decisives and kick up the withering damage.<br /> <br /> I like that its lower soak makes pre-soak damage actually matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T15:45:01-07:00","id":1416907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415533-homebrew-boss-monster-the-behemoth-of-blades?p=1416904#post1416904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it, it puts up fight but you don't NEED to cheese it. Maybe specify that clashing any attack includes attacks it's not aware of so stealthmonkeys don't have to have it to easy. <br /> <br /> It might be a little weak on damage against anyone with resistance charms. Given that you can stop fighting it at any time if you are losing it could stand at least double 10s on decisives and kick up the withering damage.<br /> <br /> I like that its lower soak makes pre-soak damage actually matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's meant to include Ambushes, so I clarified.<br /> <br /> Art of Cutting ignores Hardness, and on Base Initiative 7 with its own health regen, I thought we were pretty well covered there. But I'll throw a Resistance build against it for fine tuning.<br /> <br /> It's generally the consensus that high Soak is unfun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}